  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 109 PM MDT Tue Aug 18 2026\n\nMoving towards the end of the work week, high pressure builds in \nover the Four Corners, slowly pushing east into this weekend. \nTemperatures will warm as mid-level moisture remains, giving us \ndaily chances for showers and thunderstorms. Given the lack of \nforcing out east, most convection will remain tied to the mountains. \nFlash flooding will continue to be a primary concern over burn scars \nand other vulnerable areas, due to the potential for heavy rainfall \nseveral days in a row. Meanwhile, temperatures will continue to \nwarm, reaching mid-high 80s over the interior valleys and 90s to low-\n100s over the eastern plains.\n\nBy next week, the monsoon plume is expected to move back into our \narea, giving us a more favorable pattern for widespread showers and \nthunderstorms. Will have to see how models handle the evolution of \nthe pattern over the rest of this week, but in general conditions \nare looking wetter and a good few degrees cooler.",
